WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.540
London, 1967.

2
00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:07.470
Cicely Saunders opens St Christopher's,
the first modern hospice.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.520
Its aim is to relieve pain and distress
when a cure is no longer possible.

4
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.340
In 2002, the Netherlands
and Belgium went further.

5
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.440
There, a doctor may end a life on request,

6
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.340
under strict conditions.

7
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:26.100
So if someone in great pain asks
to die, whose life is it to end:

8
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.180
theirs, a doctor's, or God's?

9
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:33.050
In this mission, you'll sort
the cases: active or passive,

10
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.760
voluntary or not.

11
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:38.340
Then you'll compare two ways of
measuring the worth of a life,

12
00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.620
and see why the divide is not
simply religious against secular.

13
00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:45.870
Your mission: work out
whose life it is to end,

14
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.350
and why people disagree so deeply.
